# Example requests. Works with the VS Code REST Client extension and the
# JetBrains HTTP client. Run them top to bottom - each step reuses the id
# created by the previous one.

@base = http://localhost:8000
# Only needed when API_KEY is set in .env (public deployments).
@apiKey =

### 1. Health
GET {{base}}/health

### 2. Models this service can price
GET {{base}}/api/v1/models

### 3. Create a session
# @name createSession
POST {{base}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "title": "Demo session",
  "system_prompt": "Answer in one short sentence."
}

### 4. Send the first message
@sessionId = {{createSession.response.body.id}}

POST {{base}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sessionId}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "content": "My name is Oleh and my favourite number is 27."
}

### 5. Follow-up that only the stored history can answer
POST {{base}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sessionId}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "content": "What is my name and my favourite number?"
}

### 6. Full history plus accumulated cost
GET {{base}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sessionId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 6a. Answer one message with a different model
# The session default is unchanged; the cost uses this model's tariff.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sessionId}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "content": "Same question, cheaper model.",
  "model": "gpt-5-nano"
}

### 6b. Reset the session - same id, empty context, zero active cost
POST {{base}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sessionId}}/reset
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 6c. After the reset the model no longer knows the earlier context
POST {{base}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sessionId}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "content": "What is my name?"
}

### 6d. History is empty, but lifetime_cost still shows what was spent
GET {{base}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sessionId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 6e. Error case - unsupported model, rejected before any spending
POST {{base}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sessionId}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "content": "hi",
  "model": "gpt-9-imaginary"
}

### 7. Error case - unknown session
GET {{base}}/api/v1/sessions/does-not-exist
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 8. Error case - empty message
POST {{base}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sessionId}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "content": "   "
}
